---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="How Sovereign Stack curates listings, what the jurisdiction fields mean, and the advertising policy."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-8 pt-14">
    <span class="inline-block rotate-[-2deg] rounded-full border-2 border-ink bg-sky px-4 py-1.5 text-xs font-extrabold uppercase tracking-wider shadow-hard-sm">
      How this works
    </span>
    <h1 class="mt-6 text-5xl font-black tracking-tight">About</h1>

    <div class="mt-8 rounded-[20px] border-2 border-ink bg-cream p-7 shadow-hard sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">What this is</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Sovereign Stack is a curated directory of technology you can actually
        own: open-source software, self-hostable platforms, independently-domiciled
        services, and open hardware. We catalog products from the EU, the US, and
        the rest of the world — because digital sovereignty is not one country's
        project.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-6 rounded-[20px] border-2 border-ink bg-cream p-7 shadow-hard sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Methodology</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Every listing records the facts a sovereignty-minded buyer needs:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2.5 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Company domicile</strong> — the legal jurisdiction of the vendor.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Data residency</strong> — where customer data can physically reside.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">License</strong> — SPDX identifier, or Proprietary.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Self-hosting</strong> — whether you can run it on your own infrastructure.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">What it replaces</strong> — the incumbent product, so migrations are discoverable.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Listings are editorial and free. Inclusion is not for sale.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div id="advertising" class="mt-6 rounded-[20px] border-2 border-ink bg-ink p-7 text-cream shadow-hard-lg sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Advertising policy</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-cream/80">
        The directory is free to browse and free to be listed in. Revenue comes
        from clearly labeled sponsorships: spotlight cards, category banners,
        the sponsor strip, and sponsored guides. Every paid slot carries a
        <span class="rounded-full border border-amber bg-amber px-2 py-0.5 text-[11px] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-wider text-ink">Sponsored</span>
        sticker, outbound links use <code class="text-amber">rel="sponsored"</code>, and paid
        placement never changes editorial rankings.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-cream/80">
        Rankings are editorial; visibility is for sale. That line is the product.
        <a href="/advertise/" class="font-bold text-lime underline hover:text-amber">See the media kit →</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-6 rounded-[20px] border-2 border-ink bg-cream p-7 shadow-hard sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">AI access</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Every listing is published as clean semantic HTML with structured data,
        plus a machine-readable JSON feed at <a href="/api/listings.json" class="font-bold text-coral-deep underline">/api/listings.json</a>
        and a summary at <a href="/llms.txt" class="font-bold text-coral-deep underline">/llms.txt</a> for AI assistants and agents.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
